  "theorem": {
    "deterministic_nodes": "For the pinned F_17^32 row, the nodes encoded by integers 0,1,...,s are distinct finite field elements for every 385<=A<=426.",
    "nonsingular_branch": "If rank M(z0)=s for one finite node z0, row elimination gives an s-row set R with det M_R(z0)!=0; hence det M_R(Z) is a nonzero maximal minor and the regular bucket is nonsingular.",
    "setup": "Let M(Z)=H_{t,j}(u)+Z H_{t,j}(v) be a t x s finite regular Hankel pencil with s=j+1 and t>=s.",
    "singular_branch": "If rank M(z_i)<s at s+1 distinct finite nodes, then every maximal minor has degree at most s and vanishes at s+1 distinct points.  Therefore every maximal minor is identically zero and the bucket is a genuine singular residual for M5."
  },
